<title>FRANCE: Breakdown of EU grain export/import balance.</title>
<headline>Breakdown of EU grain export/import balance.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are details of EU grain export/import commitments as of March 11 in the 1996/97 campaign, July-to-June, supplied by member country officials.</p>
<p>On March 13, the EU also granted exports of 273,500 tonnes of soft wheat, 301,000 tonnes of barley, 62,460 tonnes of rye and and 1,400 tonnes of oats.</p>
<p>Figures below ('000 tonnes) are based on officially communicated certificates and are subject to revision.</p>
<p>			 ---------1996/97-------  ------1995/96-----</p>
<p>			   1 Jul96 to 11 Mar97    1 Jul95 to 11 Mar96</p>
<p>			 EXPORTS  PCT(1) IMPORTS  EXPORTS    IMPORTS</p>
<p>  Soft wheat(grain)  8,153     154     851    5,299	1,189</p>
<p>  Flour (2)	    5,038     144	11    3,510	   15</p>
<p>Food aid</p>
<p>    - grain		271	68	 -	401	    -</p>
<p>    - flour (2)	   98	63	 -	155	    -</p>
<p>Donations</p>
<p>    - grain		  0		   -	335	    -</p>
<p>    - flour (2)	   17		   -	 76	    -</p>
<p> TOTAL SOFT WHEAT   13,577     139     862    9,776	1,204</p>
<p>  Durum (grain)	  119		 428	 17	  953</p>
<p>  Semolina (3)	   308     880	 0	 35	    0</p>
<p>  Food aid		   1		   -	 68	    -</p>
<p> TOTAL DURUM WHEAT     428     357     428	120	  953</p>
<p> ALL WHEAT	    14,005     142   1,290    9,896	2,157</p>
<p>  Barley (grain)     4,947     396	31    1,249	  203</p>
<p>  Malt (4)	     2,661     121	 0    2,195	    0</p>
<p>  Donations		  0		   -	  0	    -</p>
<p> TOTAL BARLEY	  7,608     221	31    3,444	  203</p>
<p>  Maize (grain)	  148   1,345   1,552	 11	2,344</p>
<p>  Food aid		  12		   -	 40	    -</p>
<p> TOTAL MAIZE	     160     314   1,552	 51	2,344</p>
<p>  Rye (grain)	    701	48	 3    1,456	   33</p>
<p>  Rye flour (5)	    4	 6	 0	 62	    0</p>
<p>Donations</p>
<p>    - grain		  0		   -	  0	    -</p>
